  "version": "other",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) Long title (as adopted; the resolution only suspends deadlines to request a bill, and describes that bill)\n(quote) TO REQUIRE PERSONS WHO APPEAR TO VOTE IN PERSON AT A POLLING PLACE OR THE REGISTRAR'S OFFICE TO IDENTIFY THEMSELVES BY PRESENTING CERTAIN TYPES OF IDENTIFICATION TO AN ELECTION MANAGER OR THE REGISTRAR BEFORE THEY ARE ALLOWED TO VOTE;\n(section) Long title (as adopted)\n(quote) TO PROVIDE THAT PERSONS WHO WERE BORN ON OR BEFORE JUNE 30, 1944, AND WHO HAVE NOT BEEN ISSUED A VALID MISSISSIPPI DRIVER'S LICENSE, OR WHO ARE IDENTIFIED BY TWO OR MORE POLL WORKERS, SHALL NOT BE REQUIRED TO PRESENT IDENTIFICATION BEFORE THEY ARE ALLOWED TO VOTE;\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) Long title (as introduced only; removed by Senate amendment)\n(quote) TO CREATE AN EARLY VOTING PILOT PROGRAM IN ALCORN, BOLIVAR, LAUDERDALE AND WASHINGTON COUNTIES;\n(other) Resolution text: suspends the joint rules so that the bill described in the title may be drafted and considered.\n(other) Described bill: Restoration of Voting Rights Act, notice before guilty plea, felony disenfranchisement period (title only).",
